+
+Expected critical values: string `640,480,15`, string `Y8`, Boolean false, Boolean false; full dump must match corrected YAML after flattening, with the disabled nonexistent `enable_infra` allowance only. Log must show the exact three profiles and retain calibration warnings. Timeout normally returns 124: inspect normal SIGINT sensor close logs, not its exit status alone. Forced kill, wrong/missing parameter, extra publisher/profile, MIPI/Hardware Error or new power/kernel fault → STOP, preserve evidence and distinguish hardware from readback tooling. Capture continuous kernel/health logs using the runbook ownership model; interrupt only this owned publisher on faults. Matching readback only permits the next live observation; it does not qualify N3, recording or replay. Qualified external storage remains necessary for large bags.
